<%/*
  Article TL;DR + difficulty rating.

  Renders only when the post has at least one of:
    page.tldr         (short punchy summary, written by the author)
    page.summary      (hexo built-in)

  **Order**: page.tldr (author's own TL;DR) → page.summary (the author's
  `<!-- more -->` excerpt) → page.description.

  2026-11-16 changed the last one in: page.description used to be
  excluded, because at that time sync filled it from the article's
  editing-history table (「编写内容」列), and that column says what
  changed in the edit ("理顺结构与定位，修正错误写法") rather than what
  the article is about.  Task 5 of the phase-1 plan replaces those 85
  sentences with real summaries, so the reason for excluding description
  no longer holds -- and until it does, the reader sees nothing at all.

  One exception: 4 articles open their body with their own TL;DR block
  (「> **TL;DR**：……」 or a 「## TL;DR」 section).  Drawing the box for them
  too would put two TL;DRs on one page, so when the body already has one,
  the description stays out of the box.

  Difficulty: page.difficulty (1-5), default 3.
  Renders as 5 stars, filled up to the chosen level.
*/%>

<% var tldr = page.tldr || page.summary || ((page.content || '').indexOf('TL;DR') >= 0 ? '' : page.description); %>
<% if (tldr) { %>
  <div class="post-tldr">
    <div class="post-tldr__label">
      <i class="fas fa-bolt"></i>&nbsp;TL;DR
    </div>
    <div class="post-tldr__body"><%= tldr %></div>
  </div>
<% } %>

<% var diff = parseInt(page.difficulty || 3, 10); %>
<% if (diff >= 1 && diff <= 5) { %>
  <div class="post-difficulty">
    <span class="post-difficulty__label">难度</span>
    <span class="post-difficulty__stars">
      <% for (var i = 1; i <= 5; i++) { %>
        <i class="<%= i <= diff ? 'fas' : 'far' %> fa-star"></i>
      <% } %>
    </span>
    <span class="post-difficulty__text"><%= ['入门', '基础', '中等', '进阶', '专家'][diff - 1] %></span>
  </div>
<% } %>
